# Athena-only mirror list — replaces Debian's Mirrors.masterlist.
#
# The installer's mirror-selection step (choose-mirror) offers ONLY this
# entry, so the operator gets a standard mirror step that lists our repo
# and never Debian.  choose-mirror validates the chosen mirror by fetching
#   http://<Site><Archive-http>/dists/<suite>/Release
# i.e. http://140.245.198.222/asgard/dists/thor/Release  (which exists).
#
# The entry mirrors the plain-mirror shape upstream uses (Site / Country /
# Archive-architecture / Archive-http; no Type:).  A real ISO 3166 country
# (US — the repo host is US-region OCI) is given so `./mirrorlist` matches it
# against debian/iso_3166.tab and the country picker groups it correctly;
# without a Country the picker can come up empty.  The displayed country is
# cosmetic (one mirror, one country) and can be revisited.
#
# CAVEAT (see docs/plans/comp-01-choose-mirror-fork.md): host/path are
# hardcoded here, duplicating [Repo] AptSourceURL.  Follow-up: template them
# (@APT_SOURCE_HOST@/@APT_SOURCE_PATH@) and substitute from AptSourceURL at
# fork-build time (one source of truth).

Site: 140.245.198.222
Country: US United States
Archive-architecture: amd64
Archive-http: /asgard/
